Remove the broad attack-cancellation permission introduced by PR #114 wherever it is involved in starting another move.

Do not simply delete cutAttack() because other legitimate systems depend on ending attacks.

Instead, ensure calls to it occur only when the current move is actually eligible to be interrupted.

Input behavior

A new attack request made during an uncancellable attack must not restart, replace, or prematurely finish that attack.

Normal buffering should continue to function. A buffered follow-up may begin after the first attack naturally finishes, or when a legitimate cancellation window opens.

Repeatedly pressing the button for the attack already playing must not restart it or stack unlimited copies of it.

Do not introduce automatic attack chaining.

The current removal of Combo Assist must remain respected.

