FINAL PRIORITY INSTRUCTION

These are not optional balancing suggestions. They are strict gameplay rules.

The most important distinction is this:

I want to reverse the previous request that allowed attacks to be freely cancelled. I do NOT want to remove the game’s legitimate cancellation windows.

At the same time:

Non-attacking moves must be cancellable, and Deflect must explicitly be cancellable despite being internally classified as an attack.

Only the 3-second and 5-second special cooldown classes remain. They start after full release, never merely when startup begins.

Every Energy-consuming action has a universal nominal cost of 15. Ordinary projectiles, traps, summons, clones, and other qualifying gameplay objects must now consume that Energy instead of relying on the removed 0.5-second repeat cooldown.

All of these mechanics must be shared by humans and CPUs.

Implement these rules systematically, comprehensively, and permanently, without compromising existing legitimate combos or unrelated gameplay mechanics.
